Pending fix for the reviewer length limit (S2.4, code review of 2026-11-09). JavaScript finalizeReview
and POST /review allow a reviewer of 200 UTF-16 code units, while native finalize allows 200 UTF-8
bytes. So a long non-ASCII identity that the service records, such as 150 x "Ñ" (300 bytes) or 70
Devanagari letters, is refused by `avenquellis-grader finalize`. This patch makes native finalize
count UTF-16 code units, the way the native certificate parser already matches the browser's
2,048-character limit, and keeps a byte bound for text that is not UTF-8. It adds native-core cases
and finalize parity cases, and updates README.md and docs/NATIVE.md. Nothing that either side
accepts today is refused afterwards.

src/grader.cpp is pinned by edge/build-info.json to the committed WebAssembly module, so apply the
patch only together with a rebuild of that module:
  1. git apply patches/s2.4-native-reviewer-utf16-units.patch, git rm this file, and commit.
  2. From that commit, rebuild with emsdk 6.0.13 (EMSDK=/path/to/emsdk npm run build:edge, or the
     build-edge.yml workflow).
  3. node wasm/check.mjs
  4. Write that commit's SHA to edge/source-commit.txt.
  5. Commit edge/avenquellis-grader-runtime.js and .wasm, edge/build-info.json and
     edge/source-commit.txt.
  6. npm test, and ctest in a CMake build tree.
The module exports only assess, scaffold and backend-readings (wasm/bridge.cpp), so finalize cannot
be reached through it and the rebuilt module grades as before. The rebuild is needed only because
the manifest pins the hash of src/grader.cpp.
patches/c5-native-blank-unicode.patch waits for the same rebuild. The two patches are independent
and apply in either order: apply both in step 1 and rebuild once. If README.md or docs/NATIVE.md
has changed since, add --exclude=README.md or --exclude=docs/NATIVE.md and correct the sentence
about the reviewer limit there by hand.
Checked on copies of the fix branch, with this patch alone and with both patches in either order:
a -Werror Release build with no warnings and CTest 5/5; the new native-core and parity cases fail
without the grader change; in JavaScript only the manifest hash test fails, as expected until the
rebuild.

--- a/src/grader.cpp
+++ b/src/grader.cpp
@@ -88,9 +88,16 @@
                     std::string_view reviewer, std::string_view rationale) {
     validate(question);
     validate_answer(answer);
-    if (blank(reviewer) || reviewer.size() > 200 || blank(rationale)) {
-        throw std::invalid_argument("A reviewer (at most 200 bytes) and mathematical rationale are required.");
+    // The reviewer limit counts UTF-16 code units, as JavaScript finalizeReview does. A UTF-8 lead byte opens
+    // one unit, or two for a four-byte sequence. The byte bound also limits text that is not UTF-8.
+    std::size_t units = 0;
+    for (const char c : reviewer) {
+        const auto byte = static_cast<unsigned char>(c);
+        if ((byte & 0xc0u) != 0x80u) units += byte >= 0xf0 ? 2u : 1u;
     }
+    if (blank(reviewer) || reviewer.size() > 800 || units > 200 || blank(rationale)) {
+        throw std::invalid_argument("A reviewer (at most 200 UTF-16 code units) and mathematical rationale are required.");
+    }
     Assessment result;
     result.status = Status::human_reviewed;
     result.score = total(question, scores);
