 - `GET /health` — mode, `evaluatorConfigured` and source references; contains no secrets.
 - `POST /assess` — `{question, answer}` → offline review preparation, `status:'needs_review'`, `score:null`.
 - `POST /evaluate` — `{question, answer}` → model-assisted proposals. Only available after configuration.
-- `POST /review` — `{question, answer, criterionScores, reviewer, rationale}` → a validated human-assigned score. The supplied reviewer identity remains self-reported (`reviewerIdentityVerified:false`). The reviewer (at most 200 UTF-16 code units) and rationale must be well-formed Unicode text, so text cut inside a surrogate pair gets 400. Native `finalize` limits the reviewer to 200 UTF-8 bytes instead, so a long non-ASCII name accepted here, such as 150 × `Ñ` (300 bytes), is refused there. The optional `reviewedAt` defaults to the server time. A supplied value must use this RFC 3339 profile: `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS` with seconds `00`–`59`, an optional fraction of at most 9 digits, then `Z` or `±HH:MM`, with uppercase `T` and `Z`, for example `2026-11-09T10:00:00Z` or `2026-11-09T15:30:00.123+05:30`. Other RFC 3339 forms, namely lowercase `t` or `z`, a leap second (`:60`) and longer fractions, get 400, since JavaScript engines do not all parse the first two. The value is stored as sent.
+- `POST /review` — `{question, answer, criterionScores, reviewer, rationale}` → a validated human-assigned score. The supplied reviewer identity remains self-reported (`reviewerIdentityVerified:false`). The reviewer (at most 200 UTF-16 code units) and rationale must be well-formed Unicode text, so text cut inside a surrogate pair gets 400. Native `finalize` applies the same reviewer limit. The optional `reviewedAt` defaults to the server time. A supplied value must use this RFC 3339 profile: `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS` with seconds `00`–`59`, an optional fraction of at most 9 digits, then `Z` or `±HH:MM`, with uppercase `T` and `Z`, for example `2026-11-09T10:00:00Z` or `2026-11-09T15:30:00.123+05:30`. Other RFC 3339 forms, namely lowercase `t` or `z`, a leap second (`:60`) and longer fractions, get 400, since JavaScript engines do not all parse the first two. The value is stored as sent.
 
 All POST routes require `Content-Type: application/json`. If a service token is configured, include `Authorization: Bearer <service token>` in server-to-server requests. Public deployments refuse POST requests until the token is configured. Provider credentials and the shared service token must remain on the website's backend; do not put them in static JavaScript or browser storage. The website backend must authenticate students/teachers and authorize review actions before proxying requests. This library does not implement user accounts, a database or institution-issued credentials.
 
